      "content": "When selecting Douglas Fir beams, you should be cautious of any visible edgings, shakes, or large knots, as they can affect both strength and deflection behavior. Knots larger than 1-inch in diameter can be problematic. Look for structural defects such as splits or checks in the grain, which may indicate deeper issues within the wood. You should also ensure that the wood is sound and free from decay or insect damage. When planning the beam layout, considerations such as beam grade and relevant engineering specifications will influence your choices, and consulting with a structural engineer can provide additional insight to your specific project's requirements.",
